Refining the volatility dimension moves the premium far less than refining
x did, because the price of volatility risk is small next to the price of
persistence risk. The chain's implied persistence at one standard deviation
sits above rho on the coarse grid (0.992) and close to rho on the fine
grid (0.982), the same coarse-grid distortion direction as the
over-dispersion check. The
iteration estimate from the modulus is the right order of magnitude for a
timed run: thousands of cheap iterations.

